From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JalenLin <jalen.lin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:04:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] dt-bindings: arm: realtek: add Banana Pi BPI-W2

The RTD1296 enum only lists the Synology DS418, so a board dts using
"bananapi,bpi-w2" fails dt-validate. The RTD1395 list already carries
"bananapi,bpi-m4", so the vendor prefix and the naming are established.

Source: https://github.com/JalenLin/BPI-W2-linux

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/realtek.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/realtek.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/realtek.yaml
index be529490640c..498fa04b3e39 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/realtek.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/realtek.yaml
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ properties:
       - description: RTD1296 SoC based boards
         items:
           - enum:
+              - bananapi,bpi-w2 # Banana Pi BPI-W2
               - synology,ds418 # Synology DiskStation DS418
           - const: realtek,rtd1296
 
